In article <1tr0s0$sja@agate.berkeley.edu> datta@durban.berkeley.edu (Ruchira Datta) writes:
>What would a non-Samurai call these weapons?  These names aren't
>listed in Robert DeLoura's Weapons Guide.

Wakizashi - the smaller of the pair of swords that were the mark of rank for a
samurai (the big one being the katana).  In NH, it's a short sword for
everybody else.

Naginata - a bladed polearm, similar to the western glaive.  Carried by foot
soldiers and women in fuedal Japan.  I think it's a glaive for everyone else in
NH.

Nunchaku - a couple of sticks joined together by a chain.  A popular item in
most martial arts movies - good for nifty displays of slinging it around.  This
thing was originally an Okinawan peasent's weapon - it was derived from a
rice beater, and so their overlords couldn't arrest them for carrying a weapon,
because it was a tool after all (many weapons have this sort of origin).  In
nethack, I suspect either an Alkys or a Flail is the equivilent for
non-samurai.

